> IIRC, the only difference between the alignments as related to prayer and
> sacrifice is that chaotics must offer bigger sacrifices to get back into
> good grace when their god is angry with them.

Nope. It's true enough that chaotic gods are harder to mollify:

  if(u.ugangr) {
     u.ugangr -=
      ((value * (u.ualign.type == A_CHAOTIC ? 2 : 3)) / MAXVALUE);

(that is, your sacrifice is worth 2/3 as much as a non-chaotic's), but
sacrifices to a chaotic god do reduce prayer timeout more:

  } else if (u.ublesscnt > 0) {
    u.ublesscnt -=
      ((value * (u.ualign.type == A_CHAOTIC ? 500 : 300)) / MAXVALUE);

(that is, your sacrifice takes 5/3 as much off the prayer count - so
chaotic gods are actually easier to reconcile).

OTOH, all increases to u.ublesscnt (that is, to your prayer timeout)
involve nothing but rnz(), which in turn does not use your alignment.

